@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Clean upstream PR draft

+

+## Summary

+Add an optional built-in **Niimbot Editor** sidebar panel to Home Assistant so users can compose labels visually, preview them live, save reusable templates, and print directly from the existing `niimbot` integration.

+

+## Why

+The integration README already points users to an external browser editor for drag-and-drop label design. This patch brings that workflow into Home Assistant itself while reusing the integration's current render and print path.

+

+## What is included

+- a sidebar panel registered through Home Assistant's custom panel system

+- WebSocket endpoints for:

+  - printer listing

+  - live preview rendering

+  - direct print

+  - template list/save/delete

+- lightweight template persistence using Home Assistant storage

+- a frontend panel served from the integration

+

+## Design choices

+- **No new companion integration**. The feature lives inside `niimbot`.

+- **No service contract changes**. Existing `niimbot.print` behavior stays untouched.

+- **Minimal manifest churn**. Only `frontend` is added as a dependency so panel registration happens after the UI stack is available.

+- **No version bump in the patch**. That can be handled by the maintainer at release time.

+

+## Caveats to disclose in the PR

+- This was syntax-checked, but not run in a live Home Assistant instance here.

+- The visual editor is strongest for common payload elements. Advanced nested payloads still benefit from the YAML/JSON view and the rendered preview remains the source of truth.

+- The feature stores templates globally in HA storage, not per user.

+

+## Suggested PR title

+Add built-in Niimbot label editor panel for preview, templates, and print

